      "writtenOn": "2024-03-13T21:00:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We shouldn\u0027t use `std::vector`, it was an idea we thought we could do when graphite started, but then Herb and John\u0027s work on code size and performance makes SkTArray the better choice.\n\nAt the expense of generality, it would be convenient if we could just store a fixed size of extra bits so that `SamplerDesc` remains trivially destructible. I don\u0027t know if Dawn can commit to 4 uint32\u0027s like vulkan (seems reasonable?).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 237,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 237,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "fb3965c2acded20b0105f2f78249c3b11900601f",
