    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "819cf895_99be879e",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/vk/VulkanSamplerYcbcrConversion.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 70,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-13T21:00:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Out of curiosity, where did these limits (7 in particular) come from? Looking at the vulkan spec, I\u0027d think we could fit `fYcbcrModel` into 3 bits (it seems to have 5 unique values), and everything else needs 1 bit each so the whole thing could fit into 8 bits.\n\nThis could allow us to pack the ycbcr info into the upper 8 bits of `fFormat` if we played some games with the format extensions. Base formats seem to be small, and the extras are all shifted by a large offset (1,000,000,000+). If we subtracted this value, the formats would still be unique and then fit into 24 bits.\n\nI wish we could find some guarantees about how large a value `externalFormat` might take. If it could fit into 32-bits we could have a way of sharing storage between format and externalFormat, since only one of them is valid at a time. We\u0027d just need 1 bit (probably sign bit) to say which is which.\n\nAnyways, I don\u0027t think any of this should be considered a blocker, but more optimization potential to keep the key size and the SamplerDesc size smaller.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 65,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 70,
        "endChar": 60
      },
      "revId": "fb3965c2acded20b0105f2f78249c3b11900601f",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
